{"version":1,"slug":"Others__SSC_Super_Practice_42113_(20Q)","path":"Others/SSC Super Practice 42113 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Others","category":"SSC Super Practice 42113 (20Q).html","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In how many ways can 15 differently coloured chairs are attached to a round swing?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354; &#2333;&#2370;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 15 &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2352;&#2306;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">105*13!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">105*13!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7*13!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7*13!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15!</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>In a round swing, clockwise and anticlockwise arrangements are the same.</p><p>Total number of ways = (15  -  1)!/2 = 14!/2 = 7*13!</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A team of 5 members is to be chosen from a group of 6 male employees and 5 female employees. In how many ways 3 male employees and 2 female employees of the team can be choose?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>6 &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 5 &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2360;&#2375; 5 &#2360;&#2342;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; 3 &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 2 &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3600</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3600</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2400</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2400</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2800</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2800</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Total number of male and female employees are 6 and 5 respectively.</p><p>Total number of ways in which 5 members of the team can be choose = <sup>6</sup>C<sub>3</sub> * <sup>5</sup>C<sub>2</sub></p><p>= (6!/3!) * (5!/3!)</p><p>= [(6*5*4*3*2*1)/(3*2*1)] * [(5*4*3*2*1)/(3*2*1)]</p><p>= 120 * 20</p><p>= 2400</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>3 analog watches are selected from 7 distinct analog watches and 2 digital watches are selected from 9 distinct digital watches. In how many ways can the 5 watches be arranged in a box if the watches placed alternate.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>7 &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2319;&#2344;&#2366;&#2354;&#2377;&#2327; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 3 &#2319;&#2344;&#2366;&#2354;&#2377;&#2327; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 9 &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2337;&#2367;&#2332;&#2367;&#2335;&#2354; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 2 &#2337;&#2367;&#2332;&#2367;&#2335;&#2354; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325;-&#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2379; 5 &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">12096</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12096</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15120</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15120</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10080</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10080</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">17280</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">17280</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Total analog and digital watches are 7 and 9 respectively.</p><p>Total number of ways to select 3 analog watches and 2 digital watches when the watches placed alternate = <sup>7</sup>P<sub>3</sub> * <sup>9</sup>P<sub>2</sub></p><p>= (7!/4!) * (9!/7!)</p><p>= 9*8*7*6*5</p><p>= 15120</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many different words of 10 letters are possible using the letters of the word TELEVISION if it contains two I's together?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>TELEVISION &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; 10 &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2311;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; I &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2361;&#2379;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">36*7!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36*7!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5*9!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5*9!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18*7!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18*7!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4*7!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4*7!</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>In the word TELEVISION, there are 10 letters =&gt; 2I (which are together so count as one place), 2E are repeated.</p><p>Total number of ways = 9!/2! = 36*7!</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many different words of 12 letters are possible using the letters of the word SURVEILLANCE if the word begins and ends with E?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; SURVEILLANCE &#2325;&#2368; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; E &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; 12 &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">10!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6*11!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6*11!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5*9!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5*9!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">55*9!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">55*9!</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>In the word SURVEILLANCE, there are 12 letters =&gt; 2E (which are fix at the beginning and end), 2L are repeated.</p><p>Total number of ways = 10!/2! = 5*9!</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Three glass mugs are selected from six distinct glass mugs and a ceramic mug are selected from eight distinct ceramic mugs. In how many ways can the four mugs be arranged on a rack in a coffee shop if a glass mug must be placed at the beginning of the rack?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2331;&#2361; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2327;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360; &#2350;&#2327; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360; &#2350;&#2327; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2336; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2327; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2327; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2377;&#2347;&#2364;&#2368; &#2358;&#2377;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2309;&#2327;&#2352; &#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360; &#2350;&#2327; &#2352;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">2880</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2880</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1440</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1440</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1920</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1920</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1600</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1600</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Total glass and ceramic mugs are 6 and 8 respectively.</p><p>Total number of ways to select 3 glass mugs and a ceramic mug when a glass mug placed at the beginning of the rack = 3 * <sup>5</sup>C<sub>2</sub> * <sup>8</sup>C<sub>1</sub> * 3!</p><p>= 3 * [(5*4)/(2*1)] * 8 * 3!</p><p>= 3*10*8*6</p><p>= 1440</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a game of poker, a hand consists of 4 cards dealt from a standard deck of 52 cards. How many such hands contain exactly 1 jack and 3 Queens?\"</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2379;&#2325;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2326;&#2375;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 52 &#2346;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2325; &#2337;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; 4 &#2346;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2320;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2361;&#2366;&#2341; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2336;&#2368;&#2325; 1 &#2332;&#2376;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; 3 &#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?\"</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>A standard deck of 52 cards has 4 jacks and 4 Queens.</p><p>Total number of ways = <sup>4</sup>C<sub>1</sub> * <sup>4</sup>C<sub>3</sub> = 4*4 = 16</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A team of 7 students is to be chosen from a group of 5 boys and 4 girls. How many teams are possible if one particular boy must be excluded from the team?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>5 &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 4 &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 7 &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352; &#2352;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">8!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Students when a particular boy excluded = (5  -  1) + 4 = 8</p><p>Total number of ways = <sup>8</sup>C<sub>7</sub> = <sup>8</sup>C<sub>1</sub> = 8</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In how many ways can a football team of 9 players be chosen from 14 players?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>14 &#2326;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 9 &#2326;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335;&#2348;&#2377;&#2354; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1890</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1890</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2002</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2002</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1996</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1996</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2140</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2140</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Total number of ways = <sup>14</sup>C<sub>9</sub> = <sup>14</sup>C<sub>5</sub> = 14*13*12*11*10/(5*4*3*2*1) = 2002</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>9 men and 3 women sit at a round table. In how many ways can they sit if 3 women must sit together?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>9 &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; 3 &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 3 &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">2!*8!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2!*8!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3!*8!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3!*8!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3!*9!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3!*9!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2!*9!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2!*9!</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Number of men = 9</p><p>Number of women = 3</p><p>Total number of ways = 3! * 9!</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>8 girls and 8 boys sit on a round swing having only 16 chairs. In how many ways can they sit if they sit on alternate chairs?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>8 &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2324;&#2352; 8 &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354; &#2333;&#2370;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; 16 &#2325;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;-&#2348;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">16!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8!*8!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8!*8!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7!*8!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7!*8!</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Number of boys = 8</p><p>Number of girls = 8</p><p>Total number of ways = (8  -  1)! * 8! = 7!*8!</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many 5 digits odd numbers can be formed by using digits 1, 6, 4, 5, 7?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 1, 6, 4, 5, 7 &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; 5 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">60</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">48</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">48</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">84</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">84</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">72</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">72</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Odd digits = 1, 5, 7</p><p>Total number of ways = <sup>4</sup>P<sub>4</sub> * <sup>3</sup>P<sub>1</sub> = 24 * 3 = 72</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many different arrangements of the word CREATION are possible, if they do not begin with OR?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>CREATION &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2375; OR &#2360;&#2375; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">40000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">38400</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">38400</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40800</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40800</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">39600</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">39600</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>In the word CREATION, there are 8 letters with no repetition.</p><p>Total number of ways = 8!</p><p>Total number of ways when they begin with OR = 6!</p><p>Total number of ways when they do not begin with OR = 8!  -  6! = 55*6! = 39600</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many different arrangements of the word PRESUMPTUOUS are possible?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; PRESUMPTUOUS &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">22*10!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22*10!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">55*9!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">55*9!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6*11!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6*11!</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>In the word PRESUMPTUOUS, there are 12 letters =&gt; 2P, 2S, 3U are repeated.</p><p>Total number of ways = 12!/(2! * 2! * 3!) = 55*9!</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In how many ways can 9 adults and 8 kids be arranged in a row if adults and kids are alternate?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2351;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2306;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2376;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2352;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2379; 9 &#2357;&#2351;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 8 &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">17!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">17!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9! * 8!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9! * 8!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9 * 8!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9 * 8!</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8! * 7!</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8! * 7!</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>When 9 adults and 8 kids be arranged, an adult will be on each end.</p><p>Total number of ways = 9! * 8!</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A football team consists of 11 players. In how many ways can the captain and vice-captain be chosen?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335;&#2348;&#2377;&#2354; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 11 &#2326;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2346;-&#2325;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">121</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">121</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">110</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">110</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">55</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">55</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">100</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">100</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Players in football team = 11</p><p>Total number of ways to choose the captain and vice-captain = 11*10 = 110</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many different OTP's can be possible with three numbers followed by two letters?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; OTP &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2357; &#2361;&#2379; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">10<sup>2</sup>*26<sup>3</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10<sup>2</sup>*26<sup>3</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10<sup>3</sup>*26<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10<sup>3</sup>*26<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10<sup>3</sup>*26<sup>3</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10<sup>3</sup>*26<sup>3</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10*26</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10*26</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Total single-digit numbers = 10</p><p>Total letters = 26</p><p>Total number of ways = 10*10*10*26*26= 10<sup>3</sup>*26<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>There are 10 persons and 6 seats. How many arrangements are possible if only 6 of them are seated?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; 10 &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2324;&#2352; 6 &#2360;&#2368;&#2335;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; 6 &#2361;&#2368; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">5040</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5040</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4320</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4320</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5760</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5760</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4410</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4410</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Number of persons =10</p><p>Number of seats = 6</p><p>Total number of ways = <sup>10</sup>C<sub>6</sub> = 10*9*8*7 = 5040</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the number of arrangements if a dice rolled 44 times?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366; 44 &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2369;&#2338;&#2364;&#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">6<sup>22</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6<sup>22</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6<sup>44</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6<sup>44</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6<sup>43</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6<sup>43</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6<sup>45</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6<sup>45</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>When a dic e rolled N times, the number of arrangements = 6<sup>N</sup></p><p>Number of arrangements if a die rolled 44 times = 6<sup>44</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Sheena has 5 English mock tests, 3 Reasoning mock tests and 8 Quant mock tests from which she chooses a mock test. In how many ways can she select 1 English mock test, 1 Reasoning mock test and 1 Quant mock test?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2358;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; 5 &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;, 3 &#2352;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 8 &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2306;&#2335; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2361; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 1 &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;, 1 &#2352;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 1 &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2306;&#2335; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">140</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">140</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">100</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">100</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">60</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">120</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">120</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Number of English mock tests = 5</p><p>Number of Reasoning mock tests = 3</p><p>Number of Quant mock tests = 8</p><p>Total number of ways = 5*3*8 = 120</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}